{"changes":[{"location":"Policy Period End","change_type":"structured","description":"Policy period end date moved from July 16, 2026 to September 14, 2026, lengthening the policy term.","old":"07/16/2026","new":"September 14, 2026"},{"location":"Property Damage Liability Limit","change_type":"structured","description":"Property damage liability limit cut from $100,000 to $25,000 per accident.","old":"$100,000 each accident","new":"$25,000 each accident"},{"location":"Uninsured/Underinsured Motorist Limit","change_type":"structured","description":"Uninsured/underinsured motorist limits cut from $100,000/$300,000 to $25,000/$50,000.","old":"$100,000 each person / $300,000 each accident","new":"$25,000 each person / $50,000 each accident"},{"location":"Medical Payments Limit","change_type":"structured","description":"Medical payments limit cut from $5,000 to $1,000 per person.","old":"$5,000 each person","new":"$1,000 each person"},{"location":"5.2","change_type":"clause","description":"The fraud exclusion now requires intentional misrepresentation. Knowing concealment is no longer listed as grounds for denying coverage, which narrows the exclusion.","old":"We do not provide coverage for any insured who has knowingly concealed or misrepresented any material fact or circumstance in connection with this policy or a claim.","new":"We do not provide coverage for any insured who has intentionally misrepresented any material fact or circumstance in connection with this policy or a claim."},{"location":"3.3","change_type":"clause","description":"Comprehensive theft coverage is limited to theft of the entire vehicle, so partial theft (e.g., stolen parts) is no longer listed. This narrows coverage.","old":"We will pay for direct and accidental loss to your covered auto not caused by collision, including fire, theft, vandalism, flood, and contact with animals, less the applicable deductible shown in the Declarations.","new":"We will pay for direct and accidental loss to your covered auto not caused by collision, including fire, theft of the entire vehicle, vandalism, flood, and contact with animals, less the applicable deductible shown in the Declarations."},{"location":"4.2","change_type":"clause","description":"Excess-only treatment now also applies to vehicles the insured regularly uses but does not own, which narrows primary coverage.","old":"Any insurance we provide for a vehicle you do not own is excess over any other collectible insurance.","new":"Any insurance we provide for a vehicle you do not own or regularly use is excess over any other collectible insurance."}]}
```

